README for RudeConfig
See the end of file for copying conditions


*** INTRODUCTION ***

RudeConfig is a library that allows applications to (painlessly) read,
modify, and create config / .ini files.

Full documentation, including a quick start and API notes, is in README.md.


*** BUILDING ***

RudeConfig builds with CMake:

	cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
	cmake --build build
	ctest --test-dir build
	cmake --install build

Then include <rude/config.h> and link with -lrudeconfig, or use
find_package(rudeconfig) from CMake, or pkg-config.

The autotools build (configure / Makefile.am) was removed in this release.
It had been deprecated since the CMake build landed, and its shipped
config.guess dated from 2003, so it could not configure on any ARM machine -
which today means every Apple Silicon Mac and every ARM Linux server.  If you
need it, check out the v6.0.1 tag or earlier.

See file `COPYING' for copying conditions.
See file `NEWS' for a list of major changes in the current release.
See file `THANKS' for a list of contributors.
See file 'AUTHORS' for contact information


*** BUG REPORTING ***

Please report bugs at https://github.com/mflood/rudeconfig/issues

A bug report should contain an adequate description of the problem, your
input, what you expected, what you got, and why this is wrong.  Where
applicable, please include actual data files.  Consider documentation errors
as bugs, and report them as such.

The rudeserver.com addresses and discussion forum referenced by older
releases are no longer active.


